    "long_instructions": "Some of the data is lost and can’t be counted. Currently, this lost data breaks your program: when `row[\"artifacts_found\"]` is an empty string, calling `int(row[\"artifacts_found\"])` raises a `ValueError`.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Skip counting rows if the value for `row[\"artifacts_found\"]` is lost—that is, an empty string (`\"\"`).\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRecall you can use `continue` to skip an iteration of a loop.\r\n",
